From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marco Müller <hello@annoyedmilk.ch>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:14:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(spi_flash): enable suspend for GD25Q256E (0xC84019)

The GD25Q256E (JEDEC ID C8 40 19) supports program/erase suspend (75h)
and resume (7Ah), with SUS1 at S15 and SUS2 at S10, which is what the
GD driver reads with RDSR2 (35h) and mask 0x84.  It was not in the list
of GD chips with SPI_FLASH_CHIP_CAP_SUSPEND, so with
CONFIG_SPI_FLASH_AUTO_SUSPEND esp_flash_suspend_cmd_init() returned
ESP_ERR_NOT_SUPPORTED and init_flash asserted at boot.  The Waveshare
ESP32-S31 Zero has this chip.

The chip needs tRS >= 100 us (DS-00526 Rev1.3, AC characteristics,
note 3), so CONFIG_SPI_FLASH_SUSPEND_TRS_VAL_US must be at least 100;
the default is 50.

Upstream: none (not in master on 2026-11-17)
---
 components/spi_flash/spi_flash_chip_gd.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/components/spi_flash/spi_flash_chip_gd.c b/components/spi_flash/spi_flash_chip_gd.c
index 4948a192b22..01dccc691f9 100644
--- a/components/spi_flash/spi_flash_chip_gd.c
+++ b/components/spi_flash/spi_flash_chip_gd.c
@@ -41,6 +41,7 @@ spi_flash_caps_t spi_flash_chip_gd_get_caps(esp_flash_t *chip)
     case 0xC84016:
     case 0xC84017:
     case 0xC84018:
+    case 0xC84019:
     case 0xC84319:
         caps_flags |= SPI_FLASH_CHIP_CAP_SUSPEND;
         break;
